# winebus: Adjust hatswitch encoding to follow sony gamepads, T300RS and G29, etc. (2)
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11881 state=opened
# Previous MR: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/9796

I've covered the previously missed XInput side. I guess DInput is covered by the winexinput.sys side change?

Some games (e.g., Assetto Corsa Rally 0.5.1, which is released on 2026-7-16) misinterpret \[1,8\] based hatswitch encoding.

Follow the encoding of Sony gamepads, Thrustmaster T300RS and Logitech G29 which uses 0-7 hatswitch encoding to fix that issue.

I think the game is non-compliant, but we could patch to improve compatibility.

A similar patch that I proposed landed on GE-Proton 11-6 a week ago (https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/commit/0fdd9b74b7fad38fb1c483d74efc738bb02c9e59) and there's been no reported issue about this.

Tested devices: GuliKit KK2 Pro (both XInput and DInput modes), T300RS

* `wine control joy.cpl`(with this branch of wine):
  * without the patch: works fine for all DInput, XInput, Windows.Gaming.Input submenus.
  * with the patch: no change
* Assetto Corsa Rally (Unreal engine):
  * indrictly tested with GE-Proton-11-6 that contains the patch, compared to Valve Proton 11-2 that doesn't that doesn't contain the patch.
  * Steam input is disabled by default.
  * without: works fie for GuliKit (both XInput/DInput), problem with T300RS d-pad
  * with: fixes T300RS d-pad.
* BeamNG:
  * indirectly tested as Assetto Corsa Rally
  * Steam input is disabled by default
  * without: all works fine
  * with: no change
* Dirt Rally 2.0
  * indirect
  * Steam input had to be disabled to recognize T300RS
  * without: all works fine
  * with: no change
* Nuclear Throne (GameMaker):
  * indirect
  * Steam input enabled only for GuliKit by default. doesn't matter.
  * without: It doesn't support DInput devices. Only GuliKit XInput mode worked.
  * with: no change
* Easy Delivery Co. (Unity3D)
  * indirect
  * Steam input enabled only for GuliKit by default. doesn't matter.
  * without: It didn't support T300RS, only GuliKit worked
  * with: no change
